    premise+ the design explanantia alone are determinate
        ∵ none of the other (non-null) explanantia  (viz. the natural ones) is determinate
        ∵ the default ground (1) suffices to determine (the otherwise indeterminate ‘reason’ of)
          the mundane case (of design)
        ∵ the supernatural case (the remaining case of design) itself implies a stable ground
            ∵ ex hypothesi ‘God had reason’
                ∴ it was valid reason ∴ it was grounded reason ∴ there is a ground
            ∵ (probably) it could not have been the default ground ∵ (probably) God is omniscient
            - this perhaps suffices as a determinate in this case
                ∵ it is only owing our unsurprising/expected ignorance of that stable ground
                  that we cannot state it the explicit/descriptive way one would expect for determination
                    ∴ this failure of *ours* cannot ex hypothesi detract from the case itself
